Z||000000||fldevel||06-06-2000||07:32 PM||||yea i know another stupid quarter pannel question ..  i have an 85 GT coupe and some one told me in order to take the quarter pannels off u have to remove that plastic panel behind the seat and loosen a nut behind there to take them off ..so i got the panel off with a pinched finger and some cursing an low and behold ..a solid peice of steel..no nut ...help !! <p>[This message has been edited by fldevel (edited 06-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||06-06-2000||09:14 PM||||You need to look close. There is a hole in the pillar that has the 11mm (I think it's 11mm) bolt deep inside it. There is another hole just above it that you can look through to see what you are doing. Don't freak if you drop your socket/bolt because it can be reached at the bottom.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-07-2000||09:37 AM||||I've never seen the hole (although I've never looked).  If 11mm doesn't work, try either 10mm or 13mm.  Seems like the only tools you need to work on a Fiero are 7, 10, and 13mm sockets and a T15 Torx wrench.  That and a AAA (or CAA for you folks in the Great White North) card are just about all you need in your tool bag.||||reg||1
